The Debian tools package installs 65-mars.rules in /usr/lib/udev/rules.d.
For a manual installation, copy it there and run udevadm control --reload.

Modern kernels expose the sysfs disk name as mars!RESOURCE while devtmpfs
creates /dev/mars/RESOURCE. The rule matches this escaped name and restricts
access to root (0600). Administrators can override permissions in a later
site-specific rule. No RUN helper modifies unrelated device paths.

During disposable guest validation, promote a resource, trigger/settle udev,
inspect the node's path and mode, then demote and confirm it disappears.
The old debian-udev.patch is retained only as a historical reference.
